# Data conversion between byte and mebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between byte and mebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1B to 0.0000MiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5B yields 0.0000MiB; backward, converting 1MiB to 1048576B preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5MiB yields 1572864.0B. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1B
print(forward_whole->to(MiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(forward_fractional->to(MiB))
backward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(backward_whole->to(B))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(backward_fractional->to(B))

<<< stdout
0.0000MiB
0.0000MiB
1048576B
1572864.0B

<<< stderr
